  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Pete Edochie, a veteran Nigerian actor and broadcaster, has died at the age of 79. Before his career in Nollywood, Edochie was a prominent figure in broadcasting. His death has drawn widespread condolences from across the country, including official tributes from President Bola Tinubu, who recognized Edochie’s status as one of Africa’s most celebrated thespians. Family members have confirmed that the actor had been undergoing treatment for prostate cancer for the past six years, including surgery performed abroad. Following the news of his passing, fellow actors, including Patience Ozokwor and Yul Edochie, shared public tributes honoring his character and professional influence. Additionally, there have been public suggestions from figures such as the singer Brymo urging the federal government to honor his legacy by renaming the National Theatre after the late actor.",
